sections.text:
Strong damage in a mid-air combat style, which makes it fairly easy to avoid a good amount of enemy attacks;

 One of the most accessible DPS in the game by far, able to function very well with a permanently obtainable weapon and teammates;

 Super easy to understand, pick up, and optimize. Has one of the lowest barriers to entry in terms of optimization ceiling in the game.

A focus on mid-air combat means enemies hitting Luuk out of the air can be especially bad. Make sure to be careful when engaging and dodge so you don’t plummet down;

 If Luuk swaps out of his rotation at any point, his kit completely stops functioning - quickswap is a strict impossibility as a playstyle;

 Outro buffs will almost certainly expire (if you don’t use Dash Cancels on his Golden Impale attacks to shorten his rotation - while it’s not a strict necessity with Lynae or Denia, it’s vital to keep in mind with Sanhua and is always good to learn regardless of team used;

 If you wish to use him in his best team, he’s in direct competition with Aemeath, who overall has a higher ceiling. His best teammates can easily be stolen away from him, so consider that carefully when pulling (although it is worth noting he is easily the best Sanhua user in the entire game).
